course: dictionary
lesson: 8699
title: Words from the sewing box
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A selvedge is the edge of a piece of woven cloth, made so that it does not fray or unravel. Fray means the threads come loose and start to come apart. Selvage is another spelling of the same word.
explain: When you buy cloth from a roll, you can often see the selvedge along the two long sides. «Cut the pattern parallel to the selvedge» means cut in a line that runs along the same direction as that firm edge.
explain: More widely, selvedge can mean any edge or border strip, such as the edge of a piece of land. Old books use it this way: «selvedge» = edge. When you meet it, ask what fits best, then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: A selvedge is the edge of woven cloth.
fact: «Selvedge» and «selvage» are two spellings of the same word.
fact: A selvedge is made so that it does not fray or unravel.
fact: «Selvedge» can also mean a border strip, like the edge of a piece of land.
fact: Check by swapping: «the selvedge of the cloth» becomes «the edge of the cloth», and the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The shop cut the cloth from a roll, and the selvedge stopped the edge from fraying.» What does selvedge mean? | A pair of scissors | *The edge of the cloth that stops it fraying | A coloured thread | The middle of the cloth
exercise: «Ella ran her finger along the selvedge, feeling for the firm edge.» Where would you find a selvedge? | Inside a loaf of bread | At the top of a tree | *On the edge of woven cloth | In the sky
exercise: «The farmer walked along the selvedge of the field.» What does selvedge mean here? | The crop growing in the middle | *The border or edge of the field | A gate into the field | A river running through it
test: Which word is another spelling of selvedge? | selfish | sandwich | *selvage | silver
test: Old books use «selvedge» = edge. Which word could replace selvedge in «the selvedge of the page»? | colour | *edge | flower | weight
exam: Jayden asks, «Is selvedge the same as selvage?» What is the answer? | No, selvedge means a colour | No, one is a sewing word and one is a fish | No, selvage means a piece of land only | *Yes, they are two spellings of the same word
